Modifications by Corepass
=========================

The skills under `skills/` are derived from `datadog-labs/cursor-plugin`
(https://github.com/datadog-labs/cursor-plugin) at commit 7136415, licensed
under Apache-2.0, and have been MODIFIED. Per Apache-2.0 section 4(b) each
modified file carries its own change notice; the changes as a set are:

- The MCP server is addressed as `datadog__datadog` (tools
  `mcp__datadog__datadog__*`) instead of Cursor's `plugin-datadog-datadog`.
- The `.dd_cursor_mcp.json` registration file, its `${DD_MCP_DOMAIN:-…}` /
  `${DD_MCP_TOOLSETS:-…}` shell-style templating, and every procedure that has
  the agent read or rewrite that file have been removed. Corepass expands
  `${VAR}` in request headers only, never in a server URL, and an agent cannot
  reach an installed plugin's own directory (outside the workspace sandbox, and
  `plugins/` is a reserved path in a managed root). Site and toolset changes are
  therefore documented as user actions.
- Cursor-specific UI instructions ("Developer: Reload Window", "Cursor Settings:
  Tools & MCP") are replaced with Corepass equivalents.
- `ddsetup`'s first-time setup procedure is dropped: this plugin ships a working
  default endpoint, so the only remaining step is connecting the server.

Upstream files vendored unmodified: `LICENSE`. The upstream `NOTICE` text is
preserved verbatim above this separator.

Not vendored: `.github/` (CI, release workflow, issue and PR templates,
dependabot, CODEOWNERS), `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json` and
`.dd_cursor_mcp.json` — repository tooling and Cursor-runtime files with no role
in this marketplace copy.
